},{"h":"More from Southern American cuisine","links":[["Ambrosia (fruit salad)","dish/ambrosia-fruit-salad"],["Barbecue bologna","dish/barbecue-bologna"],["Chess pie","dish/chess-pie"],["Chicken Maryland","dish/chicken-maryland"],["Chitlins","dish/chitlins"],["Conecuh Sausage","dish/conecuh-sausage"],["Grape hull pie","dish/grape-hull-pie"],["Hash (stew)","dish/hash-stew"],["Mississippi mud pie","dish/mississippi-mud-pie"],["Monroe Sausage","dish/monroe-sausage"],["Moon Pie","dish/moon-pie"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/75/Lemon-pepper-wings-01.png/500px-Lemon-pepper-wings-01.png","w":500,"h":366,"by":"punctuated","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lemon-pepper-wings-01.png"}},"dish/mince-pie":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/mince-pie","n":"Mince pie","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A mince pie is a sweet pie of English origin filled with mincemeat: a mixture of fruits, nuts, spices and a spirit—usually brandy—or vinegar. Also included is a fat, traditionally beef suet, although vegetable alternatives can be used. A mince pie is traditionally served during the Christmas season in much of the English-speaking world. Its history is a matter of debate but it dates back to the medieval period, possibly to the eleventh century, when returning European crusaders brought spices back with them."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-mince-pie"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mince_pie"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"],["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Mincemeat","ingredient/mincemeat"],["Shortcrust pastry","ingredient/shortcrust-pastry"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Great British Chefs: traditional British recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"greatbritishchefs.com","note":"UK chef-driven recipe site with a large section of classic British dishes.","url":"https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/features/our-most-popular-traditional-british-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"],["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"],["Chow-chow (food)","dish/chow-chow-food"],["Chowder","dish/chowder"],["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"],["Clam chowder","dish/clam-chowder"],["Clam dip","dish/clam-dip"],["Club sandwich","dish/club-sandwich"],["Cobb salad","dish/cobb-salad"],["Cobbler (food)","dish/cobbler-food"],["Cook's Corner","dish/cook-s-corner"],["Crab cake","dish/crab-cake"],["Croffle","dish/croffle"],["Dagwood Bumstead","dish/dagwood-bumstead"],["Dagwood sandwich","dish/dagwood-sandwich"],["Deep-dish pizza","dish/deep-dish-pizza"],["Desperation pie","dish/desperation-pie"],["Dirty rice","dish/dirty-rice"],["Donut hole","dish/donut-hole"],["Egg in the basket","dish/egg-in-the-basket"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/30/Mince_pies_on_a_plate.jpg/500px-Mince_pies_on_a_plate.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"christmasstockimages.com","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mince_pies_on_a_plate.jpg"}},"ingredient/instant-noodles":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/instant-noodles","n":"Instant noodles","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Instant noodles, or instant ramen, is a type of food consisting of noodles sold in a precooked and dried block with flavoring powder and/or seasoning oil. The dried noodle block was originally created by flash-frying cooked noodles, which is still the dominant method used in Asian countries; air-dried noodle blocks are favored in Western countries. Dried noodle blocks are designed to be cooked or soaked in boiling water before eating. Ramen, a Japanese adaptation of Chinese noodle soup, is sometimes used as a descriptor for instant noodle flavors by some Japanese manufacturers. It has become synonymous in the United States with all instant noodle products."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-instant-noodles"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant_noodles"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["South Korean cuisine","cuisine/south-korean-cuisine",[["Rabokki","dish/rabokki"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Ramyeon","ingredient/ramyeon"],["Tteok","ingredient/tteok"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/73/Mama_instant_noodle_block.jpg/500px-Mama_instant_noodle_block.jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"Takeaway","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mama_instant_noodle_block.jpg"}},"dish/so-tteok-so-tteok":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/so-tteok-so-tteok","n":"So-tteok-so-tteok","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from South Korean cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["So-tteok so-tteok, sometimes translated as sausage and rice cakes, is a popular South Korean street food consisting of skewered and fried garae-tteok (rice cakes) and Vienna sausages brushed with several sauces including mustard and spicy gochujang-based sauce. It is a portmanteau as well as a reduplication of sausage (소시지) and tteok (떡)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-so-tteok-so-tteok"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/So-tteok-so-tteok"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["South Korean cuisine","cuisine/south-korean-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Garae-tteok","ingredient/garae-tteok"],["Sausage","ingredient/sausage"],["Tteok","ingredient/tteok"],["Vienna sausage","ingredient/vienna-sausage"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Korean Bapsang","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"koreanbapsang.com","note":"Home-style Korean recipes from Hyosun, a Korean-American mom.","url":"https://www.koreanbapsang.com/category/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from South Korean cuisine","links":[["Chalbori-ppang","dish/chalbori-ppang"],["Chimaek","dish/chimaek"],["Croffle","dish/croffle"],["Dak-galbi","dish/dak-galbi"],["Gilgeori toast","dish/gilgeori-toast"],["Hodu-gwaja","dish/hodu-gwaja"],["Hwangnam-ppang","dish/hwangnam-ppang"],["Jinju bibimbap","dish/jinju-bibimbap"],["Jjolmyeon","dish/jjolmyeon"],["Kkulppang","dish/kkulppang"],["Milmyeon","dish/milmyeon"],["Rabokki","dish/rabokki"],["Tornado potato","dish/tornado-potato"],["Ttongppang","dish/ttongppang"],["Yangnyeom chicken","dish/yangnyeom-chicken"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/73/Sotteok-sotteok.jpg/500px-Sotteok-sotteok.jpg","w":500,"h":461,"by":"Ajumeoni","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sotteok-sotteok.jpg"}},"dish/stippgrutze":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/stippgrutze","n":"Stippgrütze","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Stippgrütze, also called Wurstebrei, is a German dish from Westphalia which is similar to  Grützwurst or Knipp. It consists of barley groats cooked in sausage juices (Wurstbrühe), which are enriched with pieces of meat, offal, such as heart, kidney or liver and seasoned with spices and salt. More rarely, finely chopped onions are added. The cooked ingredients are minced after the juices have been poured off and a crumbly cake is left which is held together with fat and which sets on cooling. There are various recipes, but they all contain barley groats, fat and meat."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-stippgrutze"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stippgr%C3%BCtze"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"],["Thuringian cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine-thuringia"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Quick German Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"quick-german-recipes.com","note":"Long-running site by German-born cook Gerhild Fulson (Oma) with traditional German home recipes.","url":"https://www.quick-german-recipes.com/about-me.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Dirndl Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dirndlkitchen.com","note":"Blog of German and Bavarian recipes, from main dishes to holiday baking.","url":"https://dirndlkitchen.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Quick German Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"quick-german-recipes.com","note":"Thuringia page on German-born cook Gerhild Fulson's long-running German recipe site.","url":"https://www.quick-german-recipes.com/thuringia.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from German cuisine","links":[["Baumkuchen","dish/baumkuchen"],["Bockwurst","dish/bockwurst"],["Buchteln","dish/buchteln"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chrain","dish/chrain"],["Dampfnudel","dish/dampfnudel"],["Eel soup","dish/eel-soup"],["Egg puffs and soup pearls","dish/egg-puffs-and-soup-pearls"],["Eintopf","dish/eintopf"],["Flammekueche","dish/flammekueche"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Hamburg steak","dish/hamburg-steak"],["Hedgehog slice","dish/hedgehog-slice"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Labskaus","dish/labskaus"],["Landjäger","dish/landjager"],["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Mett","dish/mett"],["Mock turtle soup","dish/mock-turtle-soup"],["Potato pancake","dish/potato-pancake"],["Potato salad","dish/potato-salad"],["Rødgrød","dish/r-dgr-d"],["Sauerkraut","dish/sauerkraut"],["Spaghettieis","dish/spaghettieis"],["Speckkuchen","dish/speckkuchen"],["Spundekäs","dish/spundekas"],["Steckerlfisch","dish/steckerlfisch"],["Stollen","dish/stollen"],["Streuselkuchen","dish/streuselkuchen"],["Strudel","dish/strudel"],["Westfälische Rinderwurst","dish/westfalische-rinderwurst"],["Zopf","dish/zopf"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a3/Wurstebrei-1.jpg/500px-Wurstebrei-1.jpg","w":500,"h":386,"by":"Tamorlan","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.5","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wurstebrei-1.jpg"}}}